## 4. CRUD Operations Ka Working Flow

CRUD ka matlab hai **Create, Read, Update, Delete**.

| Operation | HTTP Method | Endpoint      | Kaam                                 |
| --------- | ----------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Create    | POST        | `/employee`   | Naya employee save karna             |
| Read All  | GET         | `/employee`   | Saare employees fetch karna          |
| Read One  | GET         | `/employee/1` | ID `1` wala employee fetch karna     |
| Update    | PUT         | `/employee/1` | ID `1` wale employee ko update karna |
| Delete    | DELETE      | `/employee/1` | ID `1` wale employee ko delete karna |

Update aur Delete ke liye controller mein `@PathVariable` ko URL ke `id` se correctly map karna zaroori hai.

---

## 5. Ek Line Mein Yaad Rakhein

* **Entity:** Database table ka Java representation.
* **Repository:** Database operations.
* **Service:** Business logic.
* **Service Implementation:** Service methods ki actual implementation.
* **Controller:** Client ki HTTP requests aur responses.
* **Hibernate/JPA:** Java objects aur database ke beech mapping aur persistence.
* **MySQL:** Actual data store karta hai.

**Final flow:**

```text
Postman
   ↓
Controller
   ↓
Service Interface
   ↓
Service Implementation
   ↓
Repository (JpaRepository)
   ↓
JPA / Hibernate
   ↓
MySQL Database
```

Response isi flow mein reverse direction mein aata hai.
